---
# aphrody plugin per-project settings — template.
#
# Copy this file to `.claude/aphrody.local.md` at the root of any project
# (Aphrody monorepo or not) and keep it out of Git (`.claude/*.local.md`).
# Restart Claude Code after editing so hooks reload.
#
# Every field is optional; without this file the plugin uses its defaults.

enabled: true      # false disables the plugin's PreToolUse guard (bare `bun test` in packages with vendor/) for this project
---

# Project notes (free-form)

Anything below the second `---` is free-form context the plugin's agents may
read when relevant, for example:

- which folder of the repository the agents should focus on;
- project-specific build/test gates that replace the defaults;
- a one-line description of the project for the `/status` summary.

Machine-wide settings are environment variables, not this file:

- `APHRODY_KERNEL_BIN`: path or name of the kernel binary (default `aphrody-kernel` on PATH).
- `APHRODY_PLUGIN_QUIET=1`: silence the SessionStart kernel summary.
- `APHRODY_ALLOW_BARE_BUN_TEST=1`: disable the bare `bun test` guard everywhere.
